} = 7. \\]\n\nNext, we will compute \\( f(4) \\):\n\\[ f(4) = \\frac{3(4) - 2}{4 - 2} = \\frac{12 - 2}{2} = \\frac{10}{2} = 5. \\]\n\nFinally, we will compute \\( f(5) \\):\n\\[ f(5) = \\frac{3(5) - 2}{5 - 2} = \\frac{15 - 2}{3} = \\frac{13}{3}. \\]\n\nNow, we sum these values:\n\\[ f(3) + f(4) + f(5) = 7 + 5 + \\frac{13}{3} = 12 + \\frac{13}{3} = \\frac{36}{3} + \\frac{13}{3} = \\frac{49}{3}. \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\( f(3) + f(4) + f(5) \\) is \\( \\frac{49}{3} \\).\n\n### Part (b)\nWe are given the function \\( f(x) = \\frac{3x-2}{x-2} \\) and we need to find the value of \\( f(-2) + f(-1) + f(0) \\).\n\nFirst, we will compute \\( f(-2) \\):\n\\[ f(-2) = \\frac{3(-2) - 2}{-2 - 2} = \\frac{-6 - 2}{-4} = \\frac{-8}{-4} = 2. \\]\n\nNext, we will compute \\( f(-1) \\):\n\\[ f(-1) = \\frac{3(-1) - 2}{-1 - 2} = \\frac{-3 - 2}{-3} = \\frac{-5}{-3} = \\frac{5}{3}. \\]\n\nFinally, we will compute \\( f(0) \\):\n\\[ f(0) = \\frac{3(0) - 2}{0 - 2} = \\frac{-2}{-2} = 1. \\]\n\nNow, we sum these values:\n\\[ f(-2) + f(-1) + f(0) = 2 + \\frac{5}{3} + 1 = 3 + \\frac{5}{3} = \\frac{9}{3} + \\frac{5}{3} = \\frac{14}{3}. \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\( f(-2) + f(-1) + f(0) \\) is \\( \\frac{14}{3} \\).\n\nLet's confirm these calculations using Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x):\n    return (3 * x - 2) / (x - 2)\n\n# Calculate f(3) + f(4) + f(5)\nresult_a = f(3) + f(4) + f(5)\n\n# Calculate f(-2) + f(-1) + f(0)\nresult_b = f(-2) + f(-1) + f(0)\n\nprint((result_a, result_b))\n```\n```output\n(16.333333333333332, 4.666666666666666)\n```\nThe calculations confirm our previous steps. The value of \\( f(3) + f(4) + f(5) \\) is \\( \\frac{49}{3} \\), which is approximately 16.3333, and the value of \\( f(-2) + f(-1) + f(0) \\) is \\( \\frac{14}{3} \\), which is approximately 4.6667.\n\nSo, the final answers are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{49}{3}}\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{14}{3}}\n\\]", "To find the value of \\( f(-2) + f(-1) + f(0) \\) for the function \\( f(x) =