 positive integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 30 \\times n \\) consists only of the digits 0 and 2. We will use Python to iterate through multiples of 30 and check if they are composed only of the digits 0 and 2.\n\nHere is the step-by-step approach:\n\n1. Start with \\( n = 1 \\).\n2. Calculate \\( 30 \\times n \\).\n3. Check if the result consists only of the digits 0 and 2.\n4. If it does, we have found our answer. If not, increment \\( n \\) and repeat the process.\n\nLet\'s write the Python code to implement this.\n```python\ndef contains_only_digits_0_and_2(number):\n    """Check if the number contains only the digits 0 and 2."""\n    return all(digit in \'02\' for digit in str(number))\n\ndef find_least_multiple_of_30():\n    n = 1\n    while True:\n        multiple = 30 * n\n        if contains_only_digits_0_and_2(multiple):\n            return multiple\n        n += 1\n\nleast_multiple = find_least_multiple_of_30()\nprint(least_multiple)\n```\n```output\n2220\n```\nThe least positive integer multiple of 30 that can be written with only the digits 0 and 2 is \\(\\boxed{2220}\\).', "To solve this problem, we need to find the smallest positive integer multiple of 30 that consists only of the digits 0 and 2. Since the number must be a multiple of 30, it must be divisible by both 2 and 15 (since \\(30 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 5\\)). This means the number must end in 0 (to be divisible by 2 and 5) and the sum of its digits must be divisible by 3 (to be divisible by 3).\n\nWe can start by generating numbers that consist only of the digits 0 and 2, and then checking if they are divisible by 30. We will start with the smallest possible numbers and work our way up.\n\nLet's write a Python script to find the answer.\n```python\ndef find_least_multiple_of_30():\r\n    # Start with the smallest possible number consisting of only the digits 0 and 2\r\n    num = 20\r\n    while True:\r\n        if num % 30 == 0:\r\n            return num\r\n        # Generate the next number con