((1 + r)**3 - 1) / r - 66200\n\n# Initial guess for the interest rate\ninitial_guess = 0.05\n\n# Solve for r\nr_solution = fsolve(equation, initial_guess)[0]\n\n# Convert the interest rate to a percentage\nr_percentage = r_solution * 100\nprint(r_percentage)\n```\n```output\n6.000000000000005\n```\nThe minimal compound interest rate that the savings account must provide is \\(\\boxed{6}\\)%.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the minimum compound interest rate \\( r \\) that will allow the worker to accumulate at least $66,200 by the end of the third year, given that he deposits $20,000 at the end of each year.\n\nThe formula for the future value of a series of deposits (annuity) with compound interest is given by:\n\n\\[ FV = P \\left( \\frac{(1 + r)^n - 1}{r} \\right) \\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( FV \\) is the future value of the deposits,\n- \\( P \\) is the amount of each deposit,\n- \\( r \\) is the annual interest rate (decimal),\n- \\( n \\) is the number of years.\n\nIn this problem:\n- \\( FV = 66200 \\),\n- \\( P = 20000 \\),\n- \\( n = 3 \\).\n\nWe need to find the minimum \\( r \\) such that the equation holds true. Let's set up the equation and solve for \\( r \\):\n\n\\[ 66200 = 20000 \\left( \\frac{(1 + r)^3 - 1}{r} \\right) \\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[ 66200 = 20000 \\left( \\frac{(1 + r)^3 - 1}{r} \\right) \\]\n\\[ 3.31 = \\frac{(1 + r)^3 - 1}{r} \\]\n\\[ 3.31r = (1 + r)^3 - 1 \\]\n\\[ (1 + r)^3 = 3.31r + 1 \\]\n\nWe can solve this equation iteratively using Python to find the value of \\( r \\). Let's write the code to find the solution.\n```python\nfrom scipy.optimize import fsolve\n\n# Define the equation to solve\ndef equation(r):\n    return (1 + r)**3 - 3.31*r - 1\n\n# Initial guess for the interest rate\ninitial_guess = 0.05\n\n# Solve for the interest rate\ninterest_rate = fsolve(equation, initial_guess)[0]\n\n# Convert the interest rate to a percentage\ninterest_rate_percentage = interest_rate * 100\nprint(interest_rate_percentage