 = 0.02\n\n# Calculate daily caloric requirement\ndaily_caloric_requirement = calories_in_tin / percentage_of_daily_requirement\nprint(daily_caloric_requirement)\n```\n```output\n2000.0\n```\nThe daily caloric requirement is \\(\\boxed{2000}\\) calories.", "To determine the total number of calories that fulfill a person's daily caloric requirement, we can use the given information that a snack-size tin of peaches, which has 40 calories, is 2% of the daily caloric requirement.\n\nLet's denote the total daily caloric requirement as \\( C \\). According to the problem, 40 calories is 2% of \\( C \\). This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ 40 = 0.02 \\times C \\]\n\nTo find \\( C \\), we can rearrange the equation to solve for \\( C \\):\n\\[ C = \\frac{40}{0.02} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python.\n```python\n# Given values\ncalories_in_tin = 40\npercentage_of_daily_requirement = 0.02\n\n# Calculate the total daily caloric requirement\ntotal_calories = calories_in_tin / percentage_of_daily_requirement\nprint(total_calories)\n```\n```output\n2000.0\n```\nThe total number of calories that fulfill a person's daily caloric requirement is \\(\\boxed{2000}\\).", "To find out how many calories fulfill a person's daily caloric requirement, we can set up a simple equation based on the information given. If 40 calories is 2% of the daily caloric requirement, then we can let \\( C \\) be the total daily caloric requirement. The equation becomes:\n\n\\[ 40 = 0.02 \\times C \\]\n\nWe can solve this equation for \\( C \\) by dividing both sides by 0.02:\n\n\\[ C = \\frac{40}{0.02} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\ncalories_snack = 40\npercentage_daily_requirement = 0.02\n\n# Calculate the total daily caloric requirement\ntotal_daily_calories = calories_snack / percentage_daily_requirement\nprint(total_daily_calories)\n```\n```output\n2000.0\n```\nThe total daily caloric requirement is \\(\\boxed{2000}\\) calories.",