ation \\((x-1) \\cdot f(x) = 3x^4 + x^3 - 25x^2 + 38x - 17\\).\n\nThe degree of a polynomial is the highest power of \\( x \\) in the polynomial. When we multiply a polynomial \\( f(x) \\) by \\( x-1 \\), the degree of the resulting polynomial is the degree of \\( f(x) \\) plus 1. This is because the highest degree term of \\( f(x) \\), when multiplied by \\( x \\), will result in a term with a degree one higher than the highest degree term of \\( f(x) \\).\n\nGiven that the polynomial on the right-hand side, \\( 3x^4 + x^3 - 25x^2 + 38x - 17 \\), has a degree of 4, it follows that the polynomial \\( f(x) \\) must have a degree of \\( 4 - 1 = 3 \\).\n\nLet's verify this by performing polynomial division of \\( 3x^4 + x^3 - 25x^2 + 38x - 17 \\) by \\( x-1 \\) to find \\( f(x) \\).\n\nWe can use Python to perform this division and confirm the degree of \\( f(x) \\).\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables and polynomials\nx = sp.symbols('x')\nnumerator = 3*x**4 + x**3 - 25*x**2 + 38*x - 17\ndenominator = x - 1\n\n# Perform polynomial division\nquotient, remainder = sp.div(numerator, denominator)\n\n# The quotient is the polynomial f(x)\nf_x = quotient\nprint(f_x)\n```\n```output\n3*x**3 + 4*x**2 - 21*x + 17\n```\nThe quotient obtained from the polynomial division is \\( 3x^3 + 4x^2 - 21x + 17 \\), which is the polynomial \\( f(x) \\). The degree of this polynomial is 3, as the highest power of \\( x \\) is 3.\n\nTherefore, the degree of \\( f(x) \\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To determine the degree of the polynomial \\( f(x) \\), we can start by analyzing the given equation:\n\n\\[\n(x-1) \\cdot f(x) = 3x^4 + x^3 - 25x^2 + 38x - 17.\n\\]\n\nThe degree of the polynomial on the right-hand side is 4 (since the highest power of \\( x \\) is \\( x^4 \\)). The degree of the polynomial on the left-hand side is the sum of the degrees of \\( x-1 \\) and \\( f(x) \\). Since the degree of \\( x-1 \\) is 1, the degree of \\( f(x) \\) must be \\( 4 - 1 = 3 \\).\n\nT