 + d_0 \\cdot b^0 \\]\n\nFor $58_9$:\n\\[ 58_9 = 5 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 5 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 45 + 8 = 53_{10} \\]\n\nFor $18_9$:\n\\[ 18_9 = 1 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 1 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 9 + 8 = 17_{10} \\]\n\nNow we perform the subtraction in base 10:\n\\[ 53_{10} - 17_{10} = 36_{10} \\]\n\nNext, we convert the result $36_{10}$ back to base 9. To do this, we repeatedly divide the number by 9 and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[ 36 \\div 9 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 0 \\]\n\\[ 4 \\div 9 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get $40_9$. So the final answer is:\n\\[ 58_9 - 18_9 = 40_9 \\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to convert a base 9 number (given as a string) to base 10\ndef base9_to_base10(base9_num):\n    return int(str(base9_num), 9)\n\n# Function to convert a base 10 number to base 9\ndef base10_to_base9(base10_num):\n    if base10_num == 0:\n        return "0"\n    base9_num = ""\n    while base10_num > 0:\n        base9_num = str(base10_num % 9) + base9_num\n        base10_num //= 9\n    return base9_num\n\n# Given numbers in base 9\nnum1_base9 = "58"\nnum2_base9 = "18"\n\n# Convert to base 10\nnum1_base10 = base9_to_base10(num1_base9)\nnum2_base10 = base9_to_base10(num2_base9)\n\n# Perform subtraction in base 10\nresult_base10 = num1_base10 - num2_base10\n\n# Convert the result back to base 9\nresult_base9 = base10_to_base9(result_base10)\nprint(result_base9)\n```\n```output\n40\n```\nThe result of the subtraction $58_9 - 18_9$ is $\\boxed{40_9}$.', 'To solve the problem \\(58_9 - 18_9\\) and express the answer in base 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base 9 numbers to base 10.\n2. Perform the subtraction in base 10.\n3. Convert the result back to base 9.\n\nLet\'s start by converting \\(58_9\\) and \\(18_9\\) to base 10. The general formula to convert a number from base \\(b\\) to base 10 is:\n\n\\[ \\text{number}_{10} = d_n \\cdot b^n + d_{n-1