} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.\n   \\]\n\n2. To combine the fractions, we need a common denominator. The common denominator for \\(\\cos x \\sin x\\) and \\(\\cos x\\) is \\(\\cos x \\sin x\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x} = \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x}.\n   \\]\n\n3. Recall the Pythagorean identity \\(1 - \\sin^2 x = \\cos^2 x\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos^2 x}{\\cos x \\sin x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x.\n   \\]\n\nSo the simplified expression is \\(\\cot x\\).\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, sec, sin, cos, simplify, cot\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the expression\r\nexpression = sec(x) / sin(x) - sin(x) / cos(x)\r\n\r\n# Simplify the expression\r\nsimplified_expression = simplify(expression)\r\nprint(simplified_expression)\n```\n```output\n1/tan(x)\n```\nThe simplified expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\) is indeed \\(\\cot x\\), which is equivalent to \\(\\frac{1}{\\tan x}\\).\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\cot x}\n\\]", "To simplify the given expression \\(\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}\\), we can use the fundamental trigonometric identities. Recall that \\(\\sec x = \\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\). Let's substitute this into the expression and simplify step by step.\n\nThe expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sec x}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\cos x \\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.\n\\]\n\nTo combine these terms, we need a common denominator. The common denominator is \\(\\cos x \\sin x\\). So we rewrite the second term:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = 