\n```python\n# Number of shirts, pairs of pants, and hats\nnum_shirts = 5\nnum_pants = 6\nnum_hats = 8\n\n# Total number of outfits\ntotal_outfits = num_shirts * num_pants * num_hats\nprint(total_outfits)\n```\n```output\n240\n```\nThe total number of possible outfits that can be made consisting of one shirt, one pair of pants, and one hat is \\(\\boxed{240}\\).", "To solve the equation \\(|5x - 1| = x + 3\\), we need to consider the definition of the absolute value function. The equation \\(|5x - 1| = x + 3\\) can be split into two separate cases:\n\n1. \\(5x - 1 = x + 3\\)\n2. \\(5x - 1 = -(x + 3)\\)\n\nLet's solve each case separately.\n\n### Case 1: \\(5x - 1 = x + 3\\)\n\\[\n5x - 1 = x + 3\n\\]\nSubtract \\(x\\) from both sides:\n\\[\n4x - 1 = 3\n\\]\nAdd 1 to both sides:\n\\[\n4x = 4\n\\]\nDivide by 4:\n\\[\nx = 1\n\\]\n\n### Case 2: \\(5x - 1 = -(x + 3)\\)\n\\[\n5x - 1 = -x - 3\n\\]\nAdd \\(x\\) to both sides:\n\\[\n6x - 1 = -3\n\\]\nAdd 1 to both sides:\n\\[\n6x = -2\n\\]\nDivide by 6:\n\\[\nx = -\\frac{1}{3}\n\\]\n\nNow we have two potential solutions: \\(x = 1\\) and \\(x = -\\frac{1}{3}\\). To determine which of these is the largest value that satisfies the original equation, we need to check if both solutions are valid by substituting them back into the original equation.\n\n### Check \\(x = 1\\)\n\\[\n|5(1) - 1| = 1 + 3\n\\]\n\\[\n|5 - 1| = 4\n\\]\n\\[\n|4| = 4\n\\]\n\\[\n4 = 4\n\\]\nThis is true, so \\(x = 1\\) is a valid solution.\n\n### Check \\(x = -\\frac{1}{3}\\)\n\\[\n|5\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 1| = -\\frac{1}{3} + 3\n\\]\n\\[\n\\left|-\\frac{5}{3} - 1\\right| = \\frac{8}{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\left|-\\frac{5}{3} - \\frac{3}{3}\\right| = \\frac{8}{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\left|-\\frac{8}{3}\\right| = \\frac{8}{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{8}{3}\n\\]\nThis is true, so \\(x = -\\frac{1}{3}\\) is also a valid solution.\n\nSince \\(1 > -\\frac{1}{3}\\), the largest value of \\(x\\) that satisfies the equation is \\(x = 1\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the function to check the solutions\r\ndef check_solution(x):\r\n    return abs(5 * x - 1) == x + 3\r\n\r\n# Solutions found\r\nsolutions = [1, -1/3]\r\n\r\n# Check if the solutions satisfy the original equation\r\nvalid_solutions = [x for x in solutions if check_solution(x)]\r\n\r\n# Find the largest valid solution\r\nlargest_solution = max(valid_solutions)\r\nprint(largest_solution)\n```", "To solve the equation \\( |5x - 1| = x + 3 \\), we need to consider the definition of the absolute value function. The expression \\( |5x - 1| \\) can be split into two cases:\n\n1. \\( 5x - 1 = x + 3 \\)\n2. \\( -(5x - 1) = x + 3 \\)\n\nWe will solve each case separately and then determine which solution is the largest.\n\n### Case 1: \\( 5x - 1 = x + 3 \\)\n\\[ 5x - x = 3 + 1 \\]\n\\[ 4x = 4 \\]\n\\[ x = 1 \\]\n\n### Case 2: \\( -(5x - 1) = x + 3 \\)\n\\[ -5x + 1 = x + 3 \\]\n\\[ -5x - x = 3 - 1 \\]\n\\[ -6x = 2 \\]\n\\[ x = -\\frac{1}{3} \\]\n\nNow we need to check if both solutions satisfy the original equation. We will substitute \\( x = 1 \\) and \\( x = -\\frac{1}{3} \\) back into the original equation \\( |5x - 1| = x + 3 \\).\n\n1. For \\( x = 1 \\):\n\\[ |5(1) - 1| = 1 + 3 \\]\n\\[ |5 - 1| = 4 \\]\n\\[ |4| = 4 \\]\n\\[ 4 = 4 \\]\nThis is true, so \\( x = 1 \\) is a valid solution.\n\n2. For \\( x = -\\frac{1}{3} \\):\n\\[ |5\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 1| = -\\frac{1}{3} + 3 \\]\n\\[ \\left| -\\frac{5}{3} - 1 \\right| = \\frac{8}{3} \\]\n\\[ \\left| -\\frac{5}{3} - \\frac{3}{3} \\right| = \\frac{8}{3} \\]\n\\[ \\left| -\\frac{8}{3} \\right| = \\frac{8}{3} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{8}{3} \\]\nThis is true, so \\( x = -\\frac{1}{3} \\) is also a valid solution.\n\nSince we are asked to find the largest value of \\( x \\) that satisfies the equation, the answer is \\( x = 1 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function to check the solutions\r\ndef check_solution(x):\r\n    return abs(5 * x - 1) == x + 3\r\n\r\n# Solutions from the cases\r\nsolutions = [1, -1/3]\r\n\r\n# Check which solutions are valid\r\nvalid_solutions = [x for x in solutions if check_solution(x)]\r\n\r\n# Find the largest valid solution\r\nlargest_solution = max(valid_solutions)\r\nprint(largest_solution)\n```", "To solve the equation \\(|5x - 1| = x + 3\\), we need to consider the definition of the absolute value function. The expression inside the absolute value can be either positive or negative, leading to two separate cases:\n\n1. \\(5x - 1 = x + 3\\)\n2. \\(5x - 1 = -(x + 3)\\)\n\nWe will solve each case separately and then check which solutions satisfy the original equation.\n\n### Case 1: \\(5x - 1 = x + 3\\)\n\\[5x - 1 = x + 3\\]\nSubtract \\(x\\) from both sides:\n\\[4x - 1 = 3\\]\nAdd 1 to both sides:\n\\[4x = 4\\]\nDivide by 4:\n\\[x = 1\\]\n\n### Case 2: \\(5x - 1 = -(x + 3)\\)\n\\[5x - 1 = -x - 3\\]\nAdd \\(x\\) to both sides:\n\\[6x - 1 = -3\\]\nAdd 1 to both sides:\n\\[6x = -2\\]\nDivide by 6:\n\\[x = -\\frac{1}{3}\\]\n\nNow we need to check which of these solutions satisfy the original equation \\(|5x - 1| = x + 3\\).\n\n1. For \\(x = 1\\):\n\\[|5(1) - 1| = 1 + 3 \\implies |4| = 4 \\implies 4 = 4\\]\nThis is true, so \\(x = 1\\) is a solution.\n\n2. For \\(x = -\\frac{1}{3}\\):\n\\[|5\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 1| = -\\frac{1}{3} + 3 \\implies \\left|-\\frac{5}{3} - 1\\right| = \\frac{8}{3} \\implies \\left|-\\frac{8}{3}\\right| = \\frac{8}{3} \\implies \\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{8}{3}\\]\nThis is true, so \\(x = -\\frac{1}{3}\\) is also a solution.\n\nSince we are asked to find the largest value of \\(x\\) that satisfies the equation, the answer is \\(x = 1\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function to check the solutions\r\ndef check_solution(x):\r\n    return abs(5 * x - 1) == x + 3\r\n\r\n# Solutions found from the cases\r\nsolutions = [1, -1/3]\r\n\r\n# Check which solutions satisfy the original equation\r\nvalid_solutions = [x for x in solutions if check_solution(x)]\r\n\r\n# Find the largest valid solution\r\nlargest_solution = max(valid_solutions)\r\nprint(largest_solution)\n```", "To solve the equation \\(|5x - 1| = x + 3\\), we need to consider the definition of the absolute value function. The expression \\(|5x - 1|\\) can be split into two cases:\n\n1. \\(5x - 1 = x + 3\\)\n2. \\(5x - 1 = -(x + 3)\\)\n\nWe'll solve each case separately and then check which solutions satisfy the original equation.\n\n### Case 1: \\(5x - 1 = x + 3\\)\n\n\\[5x - 1 = x + 3\\]\n\\[5x - x = 3 + 1\\]\n\\[4x = 4\\]\n\\[x = 1\\]\n\n### Case 2: \\(5x - 1 = -(x + 3)\\)\n\n\\[5x - 1 = -x - 3\\]\n\\[5x + x = -3 + 1\\]\n\\[6x = -2\\]\n\\[x = -\\frac{1}{3}\\]\n\nNow we need to check if both solutions \\(x = 1\\) and \\(x = -\\frac{1}{3}\\) satisfy the original equation \\(|5x - 1| = x + 3\\).\n\n1. For \\(x = 1\\):\n\\[|5(1) - 1| = 1 + 3\\]\n\\[|5 - 1| = 4\\]\n\\[|4| = 4\\]\n\\[4 = 4\\]\nThis is true, so \\(x = 1\\) is a valid solution.\n\n2. For \\(x = -\\frac{1}{3}\\):\n\\[|5\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 1| = -\\frac{1}{3} + 3\\]\n\\[|-\\frac{5}{3} - 1| = \\frac{8}{3}\\]\n\\[|-\\frac{5}{3} - \\frac{3}{3}| = \\frac{8}{3}\\]\n\\[|-\\frac{8}{3}| = \\frac{8}{3}\\]\n\\[\\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{8}{3}\\]\nThis is true, so \\(x = -\\frac{1}{3}\\) is also a valid solution.\n\nSince we are asked to find the largest value of \\(x\\) that satisfies the equation, the answer is \\(x = 1\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the function to check the solutions\r\ndef check_solution(x):\r\n    return abs(5 * x - 1) == x + 3\r\n\r\n# Solutions from the cases\r\nsolutions = [1, -1/3]\r\n\r\n# Check which solutions are valid\r\nvalid_solutions = [x for x in solutions if check_solution(x)]\r\n\r\n# Find the largest valid solution\r\nlargest_solution = max(valid_solutions)\r\nprint(largest_solution)\n```\n```output\n1\n```\nThe largest value of \\(x\\) that satisfies the equation \\(|5x - 1| = x + 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).", "To solve the equation \\( |5x - 1| = x + 3 \\), we need to consider the two possible cases for the absolute value:\n\n1. \\( 5x - 1 = x + 3 \\)\n2. \\( 5x - 1 = -(x + 3) \\)\n\nWe'll solve each case separately and then determine which solution is the largest.\n\n### Case 1: \\( 5x - 1 = x + 3 \\)\n\\[ 5x - x = 3 + 1 \\]\n\\[ 4x = 4 \\]\n\\[ x = 1 \\]\n\n### Case 2: \\( 5x - 1 = -(x + 3) \\)\n\\[ 5x - 1 = -x - 3 \\]\n\\[ 5x + x = -3 + 1 \\]\n\\[ 6x = -2 \\]\n\\[ x = -\\frac{1}{3} \\]\n\nSo the solutions to the equation are \\( x = 1 \\) and \\( x = -\\frac{1}{3} \\). The largest value of \\( x \\) that satisfies the equation is \\( 1 \\).\n\nLet's verify these solutions using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the function to check the solutions\r\ndef check_solution(x):\r\n    return abs(5 * x - 1) == x + 3\r\n\r\n# Solutions found\r\nsolutions = [1, -1/3]\r\n\r\n# Verify the solutions\r\nvalid_solutions = [x for x in solutions if check_solution(x)]\r\nprint((valid_solutions, max(valid_solutions)))\n```\n```output\n([1], 1)\n```\nThe valid solutions to the equation \\( |5x - 1| = x + 3 \\) are \\( x = 1 \\) and \\( x = -\\frac{1}{3} \\). The largest value of \\( x \\) that satisfies the equation is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).", 'To solve the equation \\(|5x - 1| = x + 3\\), we need to consider the definition of the absolute value function. The expression inside the absolute value can be either positive or negative, leading to two separate cases:\n\n1. \\(5x - 1 = x + 3\\)\n2. \\(5x - 1 = -(x + 3)\\)\n\nWe will solve each case separately and then determine which solution is valid by checking the original equation.\n\n### Case 1: \\(5x - 1 = x + 3\\)\n\\[\n5x - 1 = x + 3\n\\]\nSubtract \\(x\\) from both sides:\n\\[\n4x - 1 = 3\n\\]\nAdd 1 to both sides:\n\\[\n4x = 4\n\\]\nDivi