xed{-4}\\).", "To find the value of \\( y \\) such that the projection of \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ y \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}\\) onto \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is \\(\\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we can use the formula for the projection of vector \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto vector \\(\\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ y \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe projection is:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 2 \\cdot 1 + y \\cdot (-2) + (-5) \\cdot 1 = 2 - 2y - 5 = -3 - 2y\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 1^2 + (-2)^2 + 1^2 = 1 + 4 + 1 = 6\n\\]\n\nAccording to the projection formula, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{-3 - 2y}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{5}{6} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis implies:\n\\[\n\\frac{-3 - 2y}{6} = \\frac{5}{6}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( y \\):\n\\[\n-3 - 2y = 5 \\implies -2y = 8 \\implies y = -4\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this by substituting \\( y = -4 \\) back into the projection formula to ensure the result is correct.\n\nWe'll use Python to verify the calculations.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\n# Define the vectors\r\na = np.array([2, -4, -5])\r\nb = np.array([1, -2, 1])\r\n\r\n# Calculate the dot products\r\ndot_product_ab = np.dot(a, b)\r\ndot_product_bb = np.dot(b, b)\r\n\r\n# Calculate the projection\r\nprojection = (dot_product_ab / dot_product_bb) * b\r\n\r\n# Expected projection\r\nexpected_projectio