(0 + 0 + 0 + 0) \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 16 \\right| = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 16 = 8\n        \\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Coordinates of points\nD = (0, 3)\nB = (0, 0)\nE = (4, 0)\nF = (8/3, 2)\n\n# Shoelace formula to calculate the area of a quadrilateral\ndef shoelace_formula(coords):\n    n = len(coords)\n    area = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        x1, y1 = coords[i]\n        x2, y2 = coords[(i + 1) % n]\n        area += x1 * y2 - y1 * x2\n    return abs(area) / 2\n\n# List of coordinates in order\ncoordinates = [D, B, E, F]\n\n# Calculate the area\narea = shoelace_formula(coordinates)\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n8.0\n```\nThe area of quadrilateral \\(DBEF\\) is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).", 'To solve the problem, we need to find the area of quadrilateral \\(DBEF\\). The coordinates of the points are given as follows:\n- \\(A(0, 6)\\)\n- \\(B(0, 0)\\)\n- \\(C(8, 0)\\)\n- \\(D\\) is the midpoint of \\(\\overline{AB}\\), so \\(D(0, 3)\\)\n- \\(E\\) is the midpoint of \\(\\overline{BC}\\), so \\(E(4, 0)\\)\n- \\(F\\) is the intersection of \\(\\overline{AC}\\) and \\(\\overline{DE}\\).\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of \\(F\\). The equation of line \\(\\overline{AC}\\) can be determined using the points \\(A(0, 6)\\) and \\(C(8, 0)\\):\n\\[ \\text{slope of } \\overline{AC} = \\frac{0 - 6}{8 - 0} = -\\frac{3}{4} \\]\nSo the equation of the line is:\n\\[ y - 6 = -\\frac{3}{4}x \\implies y = -\\frac{3}{4}x + 6 \\]\n\nNext, we find the equation of line \\(\\overline{DE}\\). The slope of \\(\\overline{DE}\\) is:\n\\[ \\text{slope of } \\overline{DE} = \\frac{0 - 3}{4 - 0} = -\\frac{3}{4} \\]\nSo the equation of the line is:\n\\[ y - 3 = -\\frac{3}{4}x \\implies y = -\\frac{3}{4}x + 3 \\]\n\nTo find the intersection point \\(F\\), we set the equations equal to each other:\n\\[ -\\frac{3}{4}x + 6 = -\\frac{3}{4}x + 3 \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ 6 = 3 + \\frac{3}{4}x \\implies 3 = \\frac{3}{4}x \\implies x = 4 \\]\n