(\\boxed{\\frac{135}{7}}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to find the measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) where a square and a regular heptagon share a common side \\(\\overline{AD}\\).\n\n1. **Understand the Geometry:**\n   - A square has internal angles of \\(90^\\circ\\).\n   - A regular heptagon has internal angles of \\(\\frac{(7-2) \\times 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{5 \\times 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7}\\).\n\n2. **Determine the Position of Points:**\n   - Let's place the square and the heptagon in a coordinate system for simplicity. Assume \\(A\\) is at the origin \\((0, 0)\\), and \\(D\\) is at \\((1, 0)\\). The side length of the square and the heptagon is 1.\n   - The coordinates of \\(B\\) (a vertex of the square) will be \\((0, 1)\\).\n   - The coordinates of \\(C\\) (a vertex of the heptagon) will be \\((\\cos(\\theta), \\sin(\\theta))\\) where \\(\\theta\\) is the angle between the side \\(\\overline{AD}\\) and the line segment \\(\\overline{AC}\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the Angle \\( \\angle BAC \\):**\n   - The angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is the difference between the angles of the square and the heptagon at point \\(A\\).\n   - The angle between \\(\\overline{AD}\\) and \\(\\overline{AB}\\) is \\(90^\\circ\\).\n   - The angle between \\(\\overline{AD}\\) and \\(\\overline{AC}\\) is \\(\\frac{900^\\circ}{7} / 2 = \\frac{450^\\circ}{7}\\) because the angle is measured from the center of the heptagon.\n\n4. **Find the Difference:**\n   - The angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is \\(90^\\circ - \\frac{450^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{630^\\circ - 450^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{180^\\circ}{7}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the internal angle of the heptagon\nheptagon_angle = (7-2) * 180 / 7\n\n# The angle BAC is the difference between 90 degrees and half of the heptagon's internal angle\nangle_BAC = 90 - heptagon_angle / 2\n\n# Simplify the angle to a common fraction\nangle_BAC_fraction = sp.Rational(angle_BAC