y \\(-\\frac{b}{a}\\). For the polynomial \\(f(x) = x^3 - 49x^2 + 623x - 2015\\), the sum of the roots is \\(-\\frac{-49}{1} = 49\\).\n\nSince the roots of \\(g(x)\\) are the roots of \\(f(x)\\) shifted by \\(-5\\), the sum of the roots of \\(g(x)\\) will be \\(49 - 5 \\cdot 3 = 49 - 15 = 34\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Coefficients of the polynomial f(x) = x^3 - 49x^2 + 623x - 2015\ncoefficients = [1, -49, 623, -2015]\n\n# Using numpy to find the roots of the polynomial\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Find the roots of the polynomial\nroots_f = np.roots(coefficients)\n\n# The sum of the roots of f(x)\nsum_roots_f = np.sum(roots_f)\n\n# The sum of the roots of g(x) = f(x + 5) is the sum of the roots of f(x) minus 5 times the number of roots (3)\nsum_roots_g = sum_roots_f - 5 * 3\n\nprint(sum_roots_g)\n```\n```output\n34.00000000000002\n```\nThe sum of the roots of the function \\(g(x) = f(x + 5)\\) is \\(\\boxed{34}\\).", "To find the sum of the roots of the function \\(g(x) = f(x + 5)\\), we need to understand how the roots of \\(g(x)\\) relate to the roots of \\(f(x)\\).\n\n1. Let's start by finding the roots of \\(f(x)\\). The roots of \\(f(x)\\) are the values of \\(x\\) that satisfy \\(f(x) = 0\\). Since \\(g(x) = f(x + 5)\\), the roots of \\(g(x)\\) are the values of \\(x\\) that satisfy \\(g(x) = 0\\), which means \\(f(x + 5) = 0\\). If \\(r\\) is a root of \\(f(x)\\), then \\(r - 5\\) is a root of \\(g(x)\\).\n\n2. The sum of the roots of \\(f(x)\\) can be found using Vieta's formulas. For a cubic polynomial \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\), the sum of the roots is given by \\(-\\frac{b}{a}\\). For the polynomial \\(f(x) = x^3 - 49x^2 + 623x - 2015\\), the sum of the roots is \\(-\\frac{-49}{1} = 49\\).\n\n3. Since the roots of \\(g(x)\\) are \\(r_1 - 5, r_2 - 5, r_3 - 5\\) where \\(r_1, r_2, r_3\\) are the roots of \\(f(x)\\), the sum of the roots of \\(g(x)\\) is \\((r_1 - 5) + (r_2 - 5) + (r_3 - 5) = (r_1 + r_2 + r_3) - 15 = 49 - 15 = 34\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given polynomial f(x) = x^3 - 49x^2 + 623x - 2015\n# The sum of the roots of f(x) is -(-49)/1 = 49\nsum_of_roots_f = 49\n\n# The roots of g(x) = f(x + 5) are r1 - 5, r2 - 5, r3 - 5\n# So the sum of the roots of g(x) is (r1 + r2 + r3) - 15 = 49 - 15 = 34\nsum_of_roots_g = sum_of_roots_f - 15\nprint(sum_of_roots_g)\n```\n```output\n34\n```\nThe sum of the roots of \\(g(x) = f(x + 5)\\) is \\(\\boxed{34}\\).", 'Find the first two common multiples of 9 and 12. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{