tic operations:**\n   - \\(0.\\overline{7} - 0.\\overline{4} + 0.\\overline{2} = \\frac{7}{9} - \\frac{4}{9} + \\frac{2}{9}\\).\n\n3. **Combine the fractions:**\n   - \\(\\frac{7}{9} - \\frac{4}{9} + \\frac{2}{9} = \\frac{7 - 4 + 2}{9} = \\frac{5}{9}\\).\n\nSo the final answer is \\(\\frac{5}{9}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom fractions import Fraction\r\n\r\n# Convert repeating decimals to fractions\r\nfrac_7 = Fraction(7, 9)\r\nfrac_4 = Fraction(4, 9)\r\nfrac_2 = Fraction(2, 9)\r\n\r\n# Perform the arithmetic operations\r\nresult = frac_7 - frac_4 + frac_2\r\n\r\n# Display the result\r\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n5/9\n```\nThe final answer, confirmed by the Python code, is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{5}{9}}\\).", 'Compute: $0.\\overline{1}+0.\\overline{2}+0.\\overline{3}$. Express your answer as a common fraction. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{} \\boxed{}. \\boxed{} \\boxed{}. \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed