n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\frac{xyz}{xz} = \\frac{\\sqrt{24 \\cdot 48 \\cdot 72}}{48}\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\frac{xyz}{xy} = \\frac{\\sqrt{24 \\cdot 48 \\cdot 72}}{24}\n\\]\nLet's calculate the value of \\(xyz\\) first:\n\\[\nxyz = \\sqrt{24 \\cdot 48 \\cdot 72} = \\sqrt{82944} = 288\n\\]\nNow we can find \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\):\n\\[\nx = \\frac{288}{72} = 4\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\frac{288}{48} = 6\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\frac{288}{24} = 12\n\\]\nFinally, we can find \\(x + y + z\\):\n\\[\nx + y + z = 4 + 6 + 12 = 22\n\\]\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given values\nxy = 24\nxz = 48\nyz = 72\n\n# Calculate xyz\nxyz = math.sqrt(xy * xz * yz)\n\n# Calculate x, y, z\nx = xyz / yz\ny = xyz / xz\nz = xyz / xy\n\n# Calculate x + y + z\nresult = x + y + z\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n22.0\n```\nThe value of \\(x + y + z\\) is \\(\\boxed{22}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to find the values of \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\) given the equations \\(xy = 24\\), \\(xz = 48\\), and \\(yz = 72\\). Once we have these values, we can find \\(x + y + z\\).\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. Multiply the three equations together:\n   \\[\n   (xy) \\cdot (xz) \\cdot (yz) = 24 \\cdot 48 \\cdot 72\n   \\]\n   This gives us:\n   \\[\n   (xyz)^2 = 24 \\cdot 48 \\cdot 72\n   \\]\n2. Simplify the right-hand side:\n   \\[\n   24 \\cdot 48 \\cdot 72 = 24 \\cdot (24 \\cdot 2) \\cdot (24 \\cdot 3) = 24^3 \\cdot 6\n   \\]\n   So:\n   \\[\n   (xyz)^2 = 24^3 \\cdot 6\n   \\]\n3. Take the square root of both sides to find \\(xyz\\):\n   \\[\n   xyz = \\sqrt{24^3 \\cdot 6} = 24 \\sqrt{24 \\cdot 6} = 24 \\sqrt{144} = 24 \\cdot 12 = 288\n   \\]\n4. Now we can find \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\) by dividing \\(xyz\\) by the given products:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{xyz}{yz} = \\frac{288}{72} = 4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{xyz}{xz} = \\frac{288}{48} = 6\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z = \\frac{xyz}{xy} = \\frac{288}{24} = 12\n   \\]\n5. Finally, we can find \\(x + y + z\\):\n   \\