}{2} = 55 \\]\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 55 is divided by 9. This can be done using the modulo operation.\n```python\n# Calculate the sum of the first 10 positive integers\nn = 10\nsum_of_integers = n * (n + 1) // 2\n\n# Find the remainder when this sum is divided by 9\nremainder = sum_of_integers % 9\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n1\n```\nThe remainder when the sum of the first 10 positive integers (which is 55) is divided by 9 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).', 'To find the remainder when the sum of the first 10 natural numbers is divided by 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the sum of the first 10 natural numbers.\n2. Divide the sum by 9 and find the remainder.\n\nThe sum of the first \\( n \\) natural numbers is given by the formula:\n\\[ S = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} \\]\nFor \\( n = 10 \\):\n\\[ S = \\frac{10 \\cdot 11}{2} = 55 \\]\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 55 is divided by 9. We can use Python to perform this calculation.\n```python\n# Calculate the sum of the first 10 natural numbers\nn = 10\nsum_n = n * (n + 1) // 2\n\n# Find the remainder when the sum is divided by 9\nremainder = sum_n % 9\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n1\n```\nThe remainder when the sum of the first 10 natural numbers (which is 55) is divided by 9 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).', "To find the remainder when the sum of the first 10 positive integers is divided by 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the sum of the first 10 positive integers.\n2. Find the remainder when this sum is divided by 9.\n\nThe sum of the first \\( n \\) positive integers is given by the formula:\n\\[ S = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} \\]\nFor \\( n = 10 \\):\n\\[ S = \\frac{10 \\cdot 11}{2} = 55 \\]\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 55 is divided by 9. We can do this by performing the division and finding the remainder:\n\\[ 55 \\div 9 = 6 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\nSo, the remainder when 55 is divided by 9 is 1.\n\nLet's verify this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the sum of th