e first 10 positive integers and then determine the remainder when this sum is divided by 9.\n\n1. Find the sum of the first 10 positive integers:\n\n   The sum of the first \\( n \\) positive integers can be found using the formula:\n   \\[\n   S = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}\n   \\]\n   where \\( n \\) is the number of terms.\n\n   For the first 10 positive integers:\n   \\[\n   n = 10\n   \\]\n   So,\n   \\[\n   S = \\frac{10 \\times (10 + 1)}{2} = \\frac{10 \\times 11}{2} = 55\n   \\]\n\n2. Determine the remainder when 55 is divided by 9:\n\n   To find the remainder, we perform the division:\n   \\[\n   55 \\div 9 = 6 \\text{ remainder } 1\n   \\]\n   This means that when 55 is divided by 9, the remainder is 1.\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\( 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\dots + 9 + 10 \\) is divided by 9 is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]', "To solve this problem, we need to find the remainder when the sum of the first 10 positive integers is divided by 9. The sum of the first 10 positive integers can be calculated using the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n\\[ S = \\frac{n(n + 1)}{2} \\]\n\nwhere \\( n \\) is the number of terms. In this case, \\( n = 10 \\):\n\n\\[ S = \\frac{10 \\cdot 11}{2} = 55 \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the remainder when 55 is divided by 9. We can do this by performing the division and finding the remainder:\n\n\\[ 55 \\div 9 = 6 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\n\nSo, the remainder when 55 is divided by 9 is 1. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the sum of the first 10 positive integers\nn = 10\nsum_of_integers = n * (n + 1) // 2\n\n# Find the remainder when this sum is divided by 9\nremainder = sum_of_integers % 9\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n1\n```\nThe remainder when the sum of the first 10 positive integers (which is 55) is divided by 9 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).", "The sum of the first 10 positive integers can be found using the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, which is $\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}$. In this case, $n=