ons for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ x = 12 + 4 \\]\n\\[ x = 16 \\]\n\n\\[ x = -12 + 4 \\]\n\\[ x = -8 \\]\n\nSo, the possible values of \\( x \\) are \\( 16 \\) and \\( -8 \\). The product of these values is:\n\n\\[ 16 \\times (-8) = -128 \\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the possible values of x\nx1 = 16\nx2 = -8\n\n# Calculate the product of the possible values of x\nproduct = x1 * x2\nprint(product)\n```\n```output\n-128\n```\nThe product of all possible values of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", "To solve the equation \\( |x-4| - 10 = 2 \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Isolate the absolute value expression.\n2. Solve the resulting equations without the absolute value.\n3. Find the product of all possible values of \\(x\\).\n\nLet's start by isolating the absolute value expression:\n\n\\[ |x-4| - 10 = 2 \\]\n\\[ |x-4| = 12 \\]\n\nThe absolute value equation \\( |x-4| = 12 \\) means that \\( x-4 = 12 \\) or \\( x-4 = -12 \\). We can solve these two equations separately:\n\n1. \\( x-4 = 12 \\)\n\\[ x = 12 + 4 \\]\n\\[ x = 16 \\]\n\n2. \\( x-4 = -12 \\)\n\\[ x = -12 + 4 \\]\n\\[ x = -8 \\]\n\nSo, the possible values of \\(x\\) are 16 and -8. The product of these values is:\n\n\\[ 16 \\times (-8) = -128 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the possible values of x\nx1 = 16\nx2 = -8\n\n# Calculate the product of the possible values of x\nproduct = x1 * x2\nprint(product)\n```\n```output\n-128\n```\nThe product of all possible values of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", "To solve the equation \\( |x-4| - 10 = 2 \\), we first isolate the absolute value expression:\n\n\\[ |x-4| = 12 \\]\n\nThe absolute value equation \\( |x-4| = 12 \\) can be split into two separate linear equations:\n\n\\[ x-4 = 12 \\]\n\\[ x-4 = -12 \\]\n\nWe solve each equation separately:\n\n1. \\( x-4 = 12 \\)\n\\[ x = 12 + 4 \\]\n\\[ x = 16 \\]\n\n2. \\( x-4 = -12 \\)\n\\[ x = -12 + 4 \\]\n\\[ x = -8 \\]\n\nSo, the solutions to the equation are \\( x = 16 \\) and \\( x = -8 \\). The product of these solutions is:\n\n\\[ 16 \\times (-8) = -128 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this by implementing the solution in Python.\n```python\n# Solving the equation |x-4| - 10 = 2\n# Isolate the absolute value expression\n# |x-4| = 12\n# This can be split into two equations: x-4 = 12 and x-4 = -12\nsolution1 = 12 + 4\nsolution2 = -12 + 4\n\n# Calculate the product of the solutions\nproduct_of_solutions = solution1 * solution2\nprint(product_of_solutions)\n```\n```output\n-128\n```\nThe product of all possible values of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", "To solve the equation \\( |x-4| - 10 = 2 \\), we first isolate the absolute value expression:\n\n\\[ |x-4| = 12 \\]\n\nThe equation \\( |x-4| = 12 \\) can be split into two separate linear equations:\n\n1. \\( x - 4 = 12 \\)\n2. \\( x - 4 = -12 \\)\n\nWe solve each equation separately:\n\n1. \\( x - 4 = 12 \\) gives \\( x = 16 \\)\n2. \\( x - 4 = -12 \\) gives \\( x = -8 \\)\n\nSo, the possible values of \\( x \\) are \\( 16 \\) and \\( -8 \\). The product of these values is:\n\n\\[ 16 \\times (-8) = -128 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the possible values of x\nx1 = 16\nx2 = -8\n\n# Calculate the product of the possible values of x\nproduct = x1 * x2\nprint(product)\n```\n```output\n-128\n```\nThe product of all possible values of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", "To solve the equation \\( |x-4| - 10 = 2 \\), we first isolate the absolute value expression. We can do this by adding 10 to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ |x-4| = 12 \\]\n\nThe absolute value equation \\( |x-4| = 12 \\) means that \\( x-4 \\) can be either 12 or -12. Therefore, we have two cases to consider:\n\n1. \\( x-4 = 12 \\)\n2. \\( x-4 = -12 \\)\n\nWe solve each case separately:\n\n1. \\( x-4 = 12 \\)\n\\[ x = 12 + 4 \\]\n\\[ x = 16 \\]\n\n2. \\( x-4 = -12 \\)\n\\[ x = -12 + 4 \\]\n\\[ x = -8 \\]\n\nSo the two possible values for \\( x \\) are 16 and 