d to convert the time it takes for the robot to travel the length of the hallway from seconds to hours. There are 3600 seconds in an hour, so 90 seconds is:\n\\[ \\text{Time} = \\frac{90 \\text{ seconds}}{3600 \\text{ seconds/hour}} = 0.025 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\n3. Finally, we can calculate the length of the hallway by multiplying the speed of the robot by the time it takes to travel the length of the hallway:\n\\[ \\text{Length of hallway} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 400 \\text{ meters/hour} \\times 0.025 \\text{ hours} = 10 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given data\ndistance_km = 1  # distance in kilometers\ntime_hours = 2.5  # time in hours\ntime_seconds = 90  # time in seconds\n\n# Convert distance to meters and time to hours\ndistance_meters = distance_km * 1000  # convert kilometers to meters\ntime_hours_for_hallway = time_seconds / 3600  # convert seconds to hours\n\n# Calculate the speed of the robot in meters per hour\nspeed_m_per_h = distance_meters / time_hours  # speed in meters per hour\n\n# Calculate the length of the hallway\nlength_hallway_meters = speed_m_per_h * time_hours_for_hallway  # length of the hallway in meters\nprint(length_hallway_meters)\n```\n```output\n10.0\n```\nThe length of the hallway is \\(\\boxed{10}\\) meters.", 'To determine the length of the hallway, we need to first find the speed of the robot and then use that speed to calculate the distance traveled in 90 seconds.\n\n1. **Calculate the speed of the robot:**\n   - The robot takes 2.5 hours to travel 1 kilometer.\n   - Convert 2.5 hours to seconds: \\(2.5 \\text{ hours} \\times 3600 \\text{ seconds/hour} = 9000 \\text{ seconds}\\).\n   - The speed of the robot is \\(\\frac{1 \\text{ kilometer}}{9000 \\text{ seconds}} = \\frac{1000 \\text{ meters}}{9000 \\text{ seconds}} = \\frac{100}{900} \\text{ meters/second} = \\frac{1}{9} \\text{ meters/second}\\).\n\n2. **Calculate the length of the hallway:**\n   - The robot travels 