e. Since the sequence repeats every 6 terms, the 100th term will have the same value as the 4th term in the repeating cycle (because \\(100 \\mod 6 = 4\\)).\n\nThe 4th term in the repeating cycle is 3. Therefore, the remainder when the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence is divided by 4 is 3.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to find the nth Fibonacci number modulo m\r\ndef fibonacci_mod(n, m):\r\n    if n == 0:\r\n        return 0\r\n    elif n == 1:\r\n        return 1\r\n    a, b = 0, 1\r\n    for i in range(2, n+1):\r\n        a, b = b, (a + b) % m\r\n    return b\r\n\r\n# Find the 100th Fibonacci number modulo 4\r\nremainder = fibonacci_mod(100, 4)\r\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n3\n```\nThe remainder when the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence is divided by 4 is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence and then find the remainder when this term is divided by 4. However, instead of directly calculating the 100th term, we can use the property of the Fibonacci sequence modulo 4. The sequence of Fibonacci numbers modulo 4 is periodic, and we can use this periodicity to find the 100th term modulo 4.\n\nLet's first write out the first few terms of the Fibonacci sequence modulo 4:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&F_1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_2 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_3 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_4 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_5 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_6 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_8 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_9 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_{10} \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_{11} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_{12} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&\\text{and so on.}\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nWe can see that the sequence repeats every 6 terms. Therefore, to find the 100th term modulo 4, we need to find the position of 100 in the repeating cycle. Since the sequence repeats every 6 terms, we can find the remainder of 100 divided by 6:\n\n\\[\n100 \\div 6 = 16 \\text{ remainder } 4.\n\\]\n\nThis means that the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence modulo 4 is the same as the 4th term of the sequence modulo 4. From the sequence above, we can see that the 4th term modulo 4 is 3. Therefore, the remainder when the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence is divided by 4 is 3.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to find the nth Fibonacci number modulo m\ndef fibonacci_mod(n, m):\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1 or n == 2:\n        return 1\n    a, b = 1, 1\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, (a + b) % m\n    return b\n\n# Find the 100th Fibonacci number modulo 4\nremainder = fibonacci_mod(100, 4)\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n3\n```\nThe remainder when the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence is divided by 4 is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To find the remainder when the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence is divided by 4, we can use the property of modular arithmetic. Specifically, we can compute the Fibonacci sequence modulo 4 and observe if it repeats.\n\nLet's start by computing the first few terms of the Fibonacci sequence modulo 4:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&F_1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_2 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_3 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_4 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_5 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_6 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_8 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_9 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_{10} \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_{11} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&F_{12} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}, \\\\\n&\\ldots\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nWe can see that the sequence repeats every 6 terms. Therefore, to find the remainder when the 100th term is divided by 4, we need to find the remainder when 100 is divided by 6, which is 4. So, the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence modulo 4 is the same as the 4th term of the Fibonacci sequence modulo 4, which is 3.\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Function to compute the nth Fibonacci number modulo m\r\ndef fibonacci_mod(n, m):\r\n    a, b = 0, 1\r\n    for _ in range(n):\r\n        a, b = b, (a + b) % m\r\n    return a\r\n\r\n# Compute the 100th Fibonacci number modulo 4\r\nfib_100_mod_4 = fibonacci_mod(100, 4)\r\nprint(fib_100_mod_4)\n```\n```output\n3\n```\nThe remainder when the 100th term of the Fibonacci sequence is divided by 4 is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To solve the problem \\(513^2 - 487^2\\), we can use the difference of squares formula. The difference of squares formula states:\n\n\\[\na^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\n\\]\n\nIn this case, \\(a = 513\\) and \\(b = 487\\). Let's calculate it step-by-step:\n\n1. Calculate \\(a - b\\).\n2. Calculate \\(a + b\\).\n3. Multiply the results from steps 1 and 2.\n\nLet's perform these calculations using Python.\n```python\n# Define the values of a and b\na = 513\nb = 487\n\n# Calculate a - b\ndifference = a - b\n\n# Calculate a + b\nsum_value = a + b\n\n# Calculate the product of the difference and the sum\nresult = difference * sum_value\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n26000\n```\nThe value of \\(513^2 - 487^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{26000}\\).", "To solve the expression \\(513^2 - 487^2\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). In this case, \\(a = 513\\) and \\(b = 487\\). So we can rewrite the expression as:\n\\[\n513^2 - 487^2 = (513 - 487)(513 + 487)\n\\]\nNow we can calculate the values inside the parentheses:\n\\[\n513 - 487 = 26\n\\]\n\\[\n513 + 487 = 1000\n\\]\nSo the expression becomes:\n\\[\n513^2 - 487^2 = 26 \\times 1000 = 26000\n\\]\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the values\na = 513\nb = 487\n\n# Calculate the difference of squares using the formula (a^2 - b^2) = (a - b)(a + b)\nresult = (a - b) * (a + b)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n26000\n```\nThe value of \\(513^2 - 487^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{26000}\\).", "To find the value of \\(513^2 - 487^2\\), we can use the dif