e value step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n31 \\times 30 = 930\n\\]\n\\[\n930 \\times 29 = 26970\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{26970}{6} = 4495\n\\]\n\nSo, \\(\\dbinom{31}{28} = 4495\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient using the math.comb function\nn = 31\nk = 28\nbinomial_coefficient = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(binomial_coefficient)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe computed value of \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).", 'To solve \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\), we can use the formula for combinations:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, \\(n = 31\\) and \\(k = 28\\). So we have:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!(31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this expression by canceling out the common factorial terms:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29 \\times 28!}{28! \\times 3!} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{6}\n\\]\n\nNow we can calculate the value using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculate the value of the combination C(31, 28)\nfrom math import comb\n\n# Using the comb function to calculate the combination\nresult = comb(31, 28)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).', "To compute \\(\\binom{31}{28}\\), we can use the property of binomial coefficients that \\(\\binom{n}{k} = \\binom{n}{n-k}\\). This property simplifies the calculation because \\(\\binom{31}{28} = \\binom{31}{3}\\). The formula for a binomial coefficient is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nSo, \\(\\binom{31}{3} = \\frac{31!}{3!(31-3)!} = \\frac{31!}{3!28!} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\\).\n\nLet's compute this step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient using the formula\nn = 31\nk = 28\n\n#