\) implies \\( x \\leq 7.6 \\)\n2. \\( x - 2 \\geq -5.6 \\) implies \\( x \\geq -3.6 \\)\n\nCombining these two inequalities, we get \\( -3.6 \\leq x \\leq 7.6 \\). The integer values of \\( x \\) in this range are \\( -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 \\). \n\nSo, the number of integers in the solution set is \\( 11 \\).\n\nLet's write the Python code to confirm this:\n\n```python\n# Define the range of x\nx_min = -3.6\nx_max = 7.6\n\n# Find the integer values in the range\nintegers_in_range = [x for x in range(int(x_min), int(x_max) + 1) if x_min <= x <= x_max]\n\n# The number of integers in the range\nnumber_of_integers = len(integers_in_range)\nprint(number_of_integers)\n```\n```output\n11\n```\nThe number of integers in the solution set of \\( |x - 2| \\leq 5.6 \\) is \\(\\boxed{11}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the integer values that satisfy the inequality \\(|x - 2| \\leq 5.6\\). \n\nFirst, let's rewrite the absolute value inequality as a compound inequality:\n\\[\n-5.6 \\leq x - 2 \\leq 5.6\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\(x\\) by adding 2 to all parts of the inequality:\n\\[\n-5.6 + 2 \\leq x \\leq 5.6 + 2\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n-3.6 \\leq x \\leq 7.6\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find all integer values within the range \\([-3.6, 7.6]\\). We will use Python to determine these integers.\n```python\n# Define the range based on the inequality\nlower_bound = -3.6\nupper_bound = 7.6\n\n# Find all integers within this range\ninteger_solutions = [x for x in range(int(lower_bound), int(upper_bound) + 1)]\nprint(integer_solutions)\n```\n```output\n[-3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]\n```\nThe integers within the range \\([-3.6, 7.6]\\) are:\n\\[\n-3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of integers in the solution set of \\(|x - 2| \\leq 5.6\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]", "To solve the inequality \\( |x-2| \\leq 5.6 \\), we need to find the range of \\( x \\) that satisfies this condition. The inequality \\( |x-2| \