ven that the area of the equilateral triangle is \\(16\\sqrt{3}\\) square centimeters.\n   - The formula for the area of an equilateral triangle with side length \\(s\\) is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} s^2\n     \\]\n   - We can set up the equation:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} s^2 = 16\\sqrt{3}\n     \\]\n   - Solve for \\(s\\).\n\n2. **Calculate the perimeter of the equilateral triangle**:\n   - The perimeter \\(P\\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\(s\\) is:\n     \\[\n     P = 3s\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the side length of the square**:\n   - The perimeter of the square is equal to the perimeter of the equilateral triangle.\n   - The perimeter \\(P\\) of a square with side length \\(a\\) is:\n     \\[\n     P = 4a\n     \\]\n   - Set the perimeters equal and solve for \\(a\\).\n\n4. **Calculate the diagonal of the square**:\n   - The diagonal \\(d\\) of a square with side length \\(a\\) can be found using the Pythagorean theorem:\n     \\[\n     d = a\\sqrt{2}\n     \\]\n\nLet's implement this step-by-step in Python using sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the side length of the equilateral triangle\ns = sp.symbols('s')\n\n# Given area of the equilateral triangle\narea_triangle = 16 * sp.sqrt(3)\n\n# Area formula for the equilateral triangle\narea_expr = sp.sqrt(3) / 4 * s**2\n\n# Solve for the side length s\nside_length_triangle = sp.solve(area_expr - area_triangle, s)[0]\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the equilateral triangle\nperimeter_triangle = 3 * side_length_triangle\n\n# Define the side length of the square\na = sp.symbols('a')\n\n# Perimeter of the square\nperimeter_square = 4 * a\n\n# Set the perimeters equal and solve for the side length of the square\nside_length_square = sp.solve(perimeter_square - perimeter_triangle, a)[0]\n\n# Calculate the diagonal of the square\ndiagonal_square = side_length_square * sp.sqrt(2)\n\n# Print the final answer\nprint(diagonal_square)\n```\n```output\n-