00\n\n# Calculate the total score for each group\ntotal_score_80 = students_80 * score_80\ntotal_score_90 = students_90 * score_90\ntotal_score_100 = students_100 * score_100\n\n# Calculate the overall total score\noverall_total_score = total_score_80 + total_score_90 + total_score_100\n\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = students_80 + students_90 + students_100\n\n# Calculate the class average\nclass_average = overall_total_score / total_students\nprint(class_average)\n```\n```output\n84.66666666666667\n```\nThe class average (mean) on the test is \\(\\boxed{84.67}\\).", "To find the class average (mean) on the test, we need to calculate the total score of all students and then divide it by the total number of students.\n\nHere's the step-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. Calculate the total score of the 20 students who scored 80: \\(20 \\times 80\\).\n2. Calculate the total score of the 8 students who scored 90: \\(8 \\times 90\\).\n3. Calculate the total score of the 2 students who scored 100: \\(2 \\times 100\\).\n4. Sum these total scores to get the overall total score of the class.\n5. Divide the overall total score by the total number of students (30) to get the class average.\n\nLet's perform these calculations using Python.\n```python\n# Number of students and their scores\nstudents_80 = 20\nstudents_90 = 8\nstudents_100 = 2\n\n# Scores\nscore_80 = 80\nscore_90 = 90\nscore_100 = 100\n\n# Calculate the total score for each group\ntotal_score_80 = students_80 * score_80\ntotal_score_90 = students_90 * score_90\ntotal_score_100 = students_100 * score_100\n\n# Calculate the overall total score\noverall_total_score = total_score_80 + total_score_90 + total_score_100\n\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = students_80 + students_90 + students_100\n\n# Calculate the class average\nclass_average = overall_total_score / total_students\nprint(class_average)\n```\n```output\n84.66666666666667\n```\nThe class average (mean) on the test is \\(\\boxed{84.67}\\)