 + total_score_90 + total_score_100\n\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = students_80 + students_90 + students_100\n\n# Class average\nclass_average = overall_total_score / total_students\nprint(class_average)\n```\n```output\n84.0\n```\nThe class average (mean) on the test is \\(\\boxed{84.0}\\).", 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour over a time of \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we simplify \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) to a mixed number. First, we perform the division to get the whole number part:\n\n\\[ 550 \\div 4 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nSo, the mixed number is:\n\n\\[ 137 \\frac{2}{4} \\]\n\nWe can simplify \\(\\frac{2}{4}\\) to \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), so the final answer is:\n\n\\[ 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nfraction_numerator = int(fractional_part * 4)  # since the denominator is 4\n\n# Simplify the fractional part\nfrom math import gcd\ncommon_divisor = gcd(fraction_numerator, 4)\nsimplified_numerator = fraction_numerator // common_divisor\nsimplified_denominator = 4 // common_divisor\n\n# Display the result as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number} {simplified_numerator}/{simplified_denominator}" if simplified_denominator != 1 else f"{whole_number} {simplified_numerator}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel a distance of \\(\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour.', 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we need to simplify \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) to a mixed number. We do this by dividing 550 by 4 to get the whole number part and the remainder will give us the fractional part.\n\n\\[ 550 \\div 4 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nSo, \\(\\frac{550}{4} = 137 \\frac{2}{4}\\). We can simplify \\(\\frac{2}{4}\\) to \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), so the final answer is:\n\n\\[ 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 4)  # since the denominator is 4\n\n# Simplify the fractional part\nfrom math import gcd\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, 4)\nsimplified_numerator = numerator // common_divisor\nsimplified_denominator = 4 // common_divisor\n\n# Display the final answer as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number} {simplified_numerator}/{simplified_denominator}" if simplified_numerator != 0 else f"{whole_number}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour.', 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the speed is 50 miles per hour, and the time is \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. First, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow, we can substitute the values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nTo perform the multiplication, we can multiply the numerators together and the denominators together:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) by dividing the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[ \\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert the improper fraction \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) to a mixed number:\n\n\\[ 275 \\div 2 = 137 \\text{ with a remainder of } 1 \\]\n\nSo, the mixed number is \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\).\n\nTherefore, the car would travel \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. Let\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_part = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 2)  # Since the denominator is 2\n\n# Output the result as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_part} {numerator}/2"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours.', 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour over a duration of \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) into an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2\\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can substitute the speed and time into the distance formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nTo perform this multiplication, we can first simplify by dividing 50 by 4 (which is the denominator of the fraction) and then multiplying by 11:\n\n\\[ 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we need to convert the improper fraction \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) into a mixed number. To do this, we divide 275 by 2 to get the whole number part and the remainder will be the numerator of the fractional part:\n\n\\[ 275 \\div 2 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\n\nSo the mixed number is:\n\n\\[ 137\\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nThus, the car would travel \\(137\\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. Let\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 11 / 4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 2)  # since the denominator is 2\n\n# Display the result as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number}{numerator}/2"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n1371/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(137\\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. Thus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]', 'To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance traveled:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the speed is 50 miles per hour, and the time is \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. First, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can calculate the distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we need to simplify \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) to a mixed number. We can do this by dividing 550 by 4 to get the whole number part and the remainder will give us the fractional part.\n\n\\[ 550 \\div 4 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nSo, \\(\\frac{550}{4} = 137 \\frac{2}{4}\\). We can simplify \\(\\frac{2}{4}\\) to \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), so the final answer is:\n\n\\[ 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 11 / 4  # hours (which is 2 + 3/4)\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 4)  # since the denominator is 4\n\n# Simplify the fractional part\nfrom math import gcd\n\ncommon_divisor = gcd(numerator, 4)\nnumerator //= common_divisor\ndenominator = 4 // common_divisor\n\n# Output the mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number} {numerator}/{denominator}" if numerator != 0 else f"{whole_number}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\( \\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}} \\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour.', "To determine how far a car travels at a speed of 50 miles per hour over a period of \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) into an improper fraction. \n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can calculate the distance by multiplying the speed (50 miles per hour) by the time (\\(\\frac{11}{4}\\) hours):\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we simplify \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) to a mixed number. \n\n\\[ \\frac{550}{4} = 137 \\frac{2}{4} = 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nSo, the car would travel \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_part = int(distance)\nfractional_part = distance - whole_part\nfraction_numerator = int(fractional_part * 4)  # since the denominator is 4\n\nmixed_number = (whole_part, fractional_part, fraction_numerator)\n\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n(137, 0.5, 2)\n```\nThe calculation confirms that the car would travel \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours.\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]", 'To determine how far a car travels at a constant speed of 50 miles per hour over a time of \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for distance:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nFirst, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) into an improper fraction:\n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow, we can substitute the values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nWe can simplify this expression by multiplying the numerators and the denominators:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we need to convert the improper fraction \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) into a mixed number. We do this by dividing 550 by 4 to get the whole number part, and the remainder will be the numerator of the fractional part:\n\n\\[ 550 \\div 4 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nSo, the mixed number is:\