 as \\( x \\) increases.\n\n3. **Finding the Minimum Value:**\n   Since \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) is a decreasing function, the minimum value will occur at the right endpoint of the interval, which is \\( x = 15 \\). So, we need to evaluate \\( f(15) \\):\n   \\[\n   f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x) for the given interval p <= x <= 15\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the range of x from p to 15\np = 5  # Example value for p (0 < p < 15)\nx_values = range(p, 16)\n\n# Calculate the function values for each x in the range\nf_values = [f(x, p) for x in x_values]\n\n# Find the minimum value of the function in the given interval\nmin_value = min(f_values)\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\n15\n```\nThe minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\). We can break down the function into different cases based on the value of \\( x \\) relative to \\( p \\) and \\( 15 \\).\n\n1. When \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\):\n   - \\( |x - p| = x - p \\)\n   - \\( |x - 15| = 15 - x \\)\n   - \\( |x - p - 15| = 15 + p - x \\)\n\nSo, the function simplifies to:\n\\[ f(x) = (x - p) + (15 - x) + (15 + p - x) = 30 - x \\]\n\nSince \\( f(x) = 30 - x \\) is a decreasing function in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in this interval will occur at \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's evaluate \\( f(x) \\) at \\( x = 15 \\):\n\\[ f(15) = 30 - 15 = 15 \\]\n\nSo, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the func